# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Lead designer panel: build a set of leads, check they fit, look at them.

WHAT IT IS FOR
--------------
Someone who wants to know whether two 8-contact leads straddling the midline
will both sit in the dorsal epidural space at T11, or whether a 4-contact lead
can be threaded out to the left third ganglion without cutting into it, should
not have to know that the midline is x = 56.60, that the canal centre follows a
cubic in z, or that a foramen is measured by alternating ray casts. This panel
is those questions with spinboxes on them:

    pick a configuration, or add leads and set the numbers   ->  Check fit
    a green PASS or a red FAIL per lead AND for the set, with the actual
    measurements, in words
    Preview                                    ->  see them all in the open document
    Export STLs                                ->  generated_leads/<name>/

No coordinates and no centreline polynomials appear anywhere in the interface.

THREE TYPES OF LEAD, AND UP TO max_leads_per_type OF EACH
---------------------------------------------------------
A configuration is a SET. Add a dorsal, a ventral or a DRG lead with the buttons
at the top; each gets its own tab of parameters, and the catalogue's
max_leads_per_type (2 by default) is what the Add buttons stop at. The
parameters differ by type because the geometry problems differ: a dorsal or
ventral lead runs rostro-caudally along the canal and is positioned by a
vertebral level and an offset from the midline, while a DRG lead runs LATERALLY
out through a neuroforamen and is positioned by naming a ganglion. The panel
shows one set of controls or the other, never both.

CHECK FIT ANSWERS TWO QUESTIONS
-------------------------------
Each lead's own verdict -- does it fit its channel, is it inside the right
tissue, does it clear the ganglion -- and then the set's, which is the one no
single lead can answer: do any two of them occupy the same space. Two leads 1 mm
apart both fit the epidural space perfectly well and still cannot both be
implanted, so the banner is red if either kind of check fails.

INSTALL
-------
    cp src/freecad/lead_designer.FCMacro "$(python3 -c 'import FreeCAD,os;print(os.path.join(FreeCAD.getUserAppDataDir(),"Macro"))')"

    # FreeCAD's macro directory is VERSIONED -- on 26.3 it is
    #   ~/.local/share/FreeCAD/v26-3/Macro/
    # not ~/.local/share/FreeCAD/Macro/, which FreeCAD ignores entirely. Ask it
    # rather than guessing, because the path moves with the version:
    #
    #   python3 -c "import FreeCAD, os; print(os.path.join(FreeCAD.getUserAppDataDir(), 'Macro'))"
    #
    # Then, in FreeCAD: Macro -> Macros... -> select this file -> Execute.

then Macro -> Macros... -> lead_designer -> Execute. Worth putting on a toolbar
the same way as tissue_visibility.FCMacro: Tools -> Customize -> Macros, then
Tools -> Customize -> Toolbars. Re-running re-uses the same dock rather than
stacking copies; close it with the dock's own X.

Like tissue_visibility.FCMacro this needs the repo on disk -- it imports
build_lead_config, which is where all the actual work lives. REPO below is the
default; set SCS_MODELING_REPO if the checkout moves.

THE PREVIEW IS DISPOSABLE, AND NOTHING HERE EVER SAVES
------------------------------------------------------
Preview puts every lead of the set into the ACTIVE DOCUMENT as ordinary
parametric bodies inside a group called SCS_LeadPreview, replacing whatever the
last preview left. That is the whole design: there is ONE model document,
NBF_RADO-SCS.FCStd, holding anatomy only, and a lead configuration is a dozen
numbers in lead_configs.yaml plus a directory of STLs. Trying ten of them must
not mean ten copies of a 25 MB document. Explore, export the one you want, and
close the document WITHOUT SAVING -- "Remove preview" puts the tree back exactly
as it was.

"Show RADO's lead" is the same kind of disposable overlay, in its own group: it
imports the five STLs RADO ships for its own hand-placed 4-contact DRG lead, so
a generated DRG lead can be looked at beside the only independently placed one
in the model. It is not part of the anatomy and must not be saved into it.

This macro contains no save of any kind and must not grow one. A FreeCAD
document saved with no GUI running loses every ShapeAppearance in it; the panel
runs inside the GUI so that is not the failure mode here, but the rule that
nothing in this pipeline saves a model document except deliberately, by hand, is
what keeps the tissue colours alive. See make_tissue_groups.py.

WHY IT BLOCKS WHILE CHECKING
----------------------------
Checking a fit ray casts a few thousand points against several meshes and takes
two to ten seconds, more for a DRG lead than an epidural one because a foramen
is measured by iterating two ray casts rather than one. It runs on the GUI
thread with a wait cursor rather than in a worker, deliberately: FreeCAD's
document API is not thread-safe, the meshes have to be loaded in the same
interpreter, and a few seconds of freeze on a button press is a far smaller
problem than a background thread mutating a document while the user clicks in
the tree.
"""
import json
import os
import sys
import traceback

import FreeCAD
import FreeCADGui

try:
    from PySide import QtCore, QtGui, QtWidgets
except ImportError:                                     # pragma: no cover
    try:
        from PySide6 import QtCore, QtGui, QtWidgets
    except ImportError:
        from PySide2 import QtCore, QtGui, QtWidgets

REPO = os.environ.get("SCS_MODELING_REPO",
                      os.path.expanduser("~/Projects/SCS-Modeling"))
OBJECT_NAME = "SCS_LeadDesignerDock"       # so a second run re-uses the dock

CUSTOM = "— custom —"

# Colours for the verdict banner. Deliberately not the tissue colours: this is
# interface chrome, and nothing in this file may imply a material.
BANNER = {"PASS": ("#1b5e20", "#c8e6c9"),
          "WARN": ("#7a4f01", "#ffe0b2"),
          "FAIL": ("#8e0000", "#ffcdd2")}

TYPE_WORDS = {"dorsal": "Dorsal epidural", "ventral": "Ventral epidural",
              "drg": "DRG (foraminal)"}


def load_builder():
    """Import build_lead_config from the repo. Everything real lives there."""
    freecad_dir = os.path.join(REPO, "src", "freecad")
    if freecad_dir not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, freecad_dir)
    import build_lead_config
    # Reloaded on every run so editing the module and re-executing the macro
    # picks the change up; a stale copy that silently ignores your edits is a
    # miserable way to spend an afternoon.
    try:
        import importlib
        importlib.reload(build_lead_config)
    except Exception:
        pass
    return build_lead_config


def worst_of(levels):
    if "FAIL" in levels:
        return "FAIL"
    return "WARN" if "WARN" in levels else "PASS"


class LeadPage(QtWidgets.QWidget):
    """The parameters of ONE lead. Which controls exist depends on its type.

    A page owns no geometry and no verdict; it is a form that can produce the
    override dict build_lead_config.resolve_lead() layers on top of the
    catalogue. Keeping it that dumb is what stops the panel and the command line
    from drifting apart -- both go through the same resolve.
    """

    changed = QtCore.Signal()

    def __init__(self, panel, kind):
        super(LeadPage, self).__init__()
        self.panel = panel
        self.kind = kind
        self.loading = False

        form = QtWidgets.QFormLayout(self)
        form.setLabelAlignment(QtCore.Qt.AlignRight)

        self.contacts = self.spin_int("How many electrode contacts", 1, 32)
        form.addRow("Contacts", self.contacts)
        self.contact_length = self.spin("Length of each contact", 0.25, 20.0, 0.25, " mm")
        form.addRow("Contact length", self.contact_length)
        self.gap = self.spin("Insulator between neighbouring contacts", 0.0, 20.0,
                             0.25, " mm")
        form.addRow("Gap", self.gap)
        self.diameter = self.spin("Lead diameter. Khadka et al. use 1.25 mm; the "
                                  "house default is 1.30 mm", 0.2, 4.0, 0.05, " mm")
        form.addRow("Diameter", self.diameter)
        self.tail = self.spin("Plain insulator beyond the end contacts", 0.0, 30.0,
                              0.5, " mm")
        form.addRow("Tail", self.tail)

        if kind == "drg":
            self.target = QtWidgets.QComboBox()
            self.target.addItems(panel.ganglia)
            self.target.setToolTip(
                "Which dorsal root ganglion. L is the patient's LEFT, R the "
                "right, numbered rostral to caudal within each side. These are "
                "the model's own ganglion numbers, NOT lumbar levels.")
            self.target.currentIndexChanged.connect(self.touched)
            form.addRow("Target ganglion", self.target)

            self.lateral_offset = self.spin(
                "Where the centre of the contact array sits along the root, "
                "relative to the ganglion's own centre. Positive is further out "
                "along the root (distal).", -10.0, 15.0, 0.5, " mm")
            form.addRow("Array along the root", self.lateral_offset)

            self.ganglion_clearance = self.spin(
                "How far the lead surface is held off the ganglion. The lead is "
                "placed on the centre of the foramen and then lifted towards the "
                "pedicle by however much this takes -- the shift is worked out "
                "for you, and differs between foramina. 0 sits on the centre, "
                "which is what RADO's own lead does.", 0.0, 4.0, 0.25, " mm")
            form.addRow("Clearance from the ganglion", self.ganglion_clearance)

            self.y_offset = self.spin(
                "A further nudge across the foramen. Positive is DORSAL "
                "(posterior).", -4.0, 4.0, 0.25, " mm")
            form.addRow("Nudge dorsal/ventral", self.y_offset)
            self.z_offset = self.spin(
                "A further nudge along the spine. Positive is ROSTRAL (towards "
                "the head).", -6.0, 6.0, 0.25, " mm")
            form.addRow("Nudge rostral/caudal", self.z_offset)

            self.ganglion_note = QtWidgets.QLabel("")
            self.ganglion_note.setWordWrap(True)
            self.ganglion_note.setStyleSheet("color: gray;")
            form.addRow("", self.ganglion_note)
            self.target.currentIndexChanged.connect(self.describe_target)

            self.numeric = (self.contacts, self.contact_length, self.gap,
                            self.diameter, self.tail, self.lateral_offset,
                            self.ganglion_clearance, self.y_offset, self.z_offset)
        else:
            self.level = QtWidgets.QComboBox()
            self.level.addItem(CUSTOM)
            self.level.addItems(list(panel.cfg["levels"]))
            self.level.setToolTip("Vertebral level for the centre of the contact "
                                  "array. Level names are RADO's own -- see the "
                                  "caveat at the top of lead_configs.yaml.")
            self.level.currentIndexChanged.connect(self.level_picked)
            form.addRow("Level", self.level)

            self.z_center = self.spin("Rostro-caudal position of the middle of the "
                                      "contact array. Set by the level above, or "
                                      "type it directly.", 0.0, 300.0, 1.0, " mm")
            self.z_center.valueChanged.connect(self.z_edited)
            form.addRow("Position (rostro-caudal)", self.z_center)

            self.x_offset = self.spin(
                "Medial-lateral offset from the midline. POSITIVE is the patient's "
                "LEFT, negative is the right, zero is on the midline.",
                -10.0, 10.0, 0.5, " mm")
            self.x_offset.valueChanged.connect(self.describe_offset)
            form.addRow("Offset from midline", self.x_offset)

            self.offset_note = QtWidgets.QLabel("")
            self.offset_note.setStyleSheet("color: gray;")
            form.addRow("", self.offset_note)

            self.numeric = (self.contacts, self.contact_length, self.gap,
                            self.diameter, self.tail, self.z_center, self.x_offset)

        for w in self.numeric:
            w.valueChanged.connect(self.touched)

    # -- widget helpers ---------------------------------------------------
    def spin(self, tip, lo, hi, step, suffix):
        w = QtWidgets.QDoubleSpinBox()
        w.setRange(lo, hi)
        w.setSingleStep(step)
        w.setDecimals(2)
        w.setSuffix(suffix)
        w.setToolTip(tip)
        return w

    def spin_int(self, tip, lo, hi):
        w = QtWidgets.QSpinBox()
        w.setRange(lo, hi)
        w.setToolTip(tip)
        return w

    def touched(self, *_a):
        if not self.loading:
            self.changed.emit()

    def level_picked(self, _i=None):
        """Picking a level drives the position box; typing a position clears it."""
        if self.loading:
            return
        name = self.level.currentText()
        if name != CUSTOM:
            self.loading = True
            try:
                self.z_center.setValue(float(self.panel.cfg["levels"][name]))
            finally:
                self.loading = False
        self.touched()

    def z_edited(self, *_a):
        """A hand-typed position means the level combo no longer describes it."""
        if self.loading:
            return
        if self.level.currentText() != CUSTOM:
            self.loading = True
            try:
                self.level.setCurrentText(CUSTOM)
            finally:
                self.loading = False

    def describe_offset(self, *_a):
        dx = self.x_offset.value()
        if abs(dx) < 0.005:
            self.offset_note.setText("on the midline")
        else:
            self.offset_note.setText("%.2f mm to the patient's %s"
                                     % (abs(dx), "LEFT" if dx > 0 else "RIGHT"))

    def describe_target(self, *_a):
        g = self.panel.foramen.get(self.target.currentText()) if self.panel.foramen else None
        if not g:
            self.ganglion_note.setText("")
            return
        self.ganglion_note.setText(
            "%s side, ganglion centre %.1f mm from the midline; the foramen is a "
            "measurable channel from %.1f to %.1f mm out."
            % (g["side"], g["ganglion_u_centre"], g["usable_u"][0], g["usable_u"][1]))

    # -- reading and writing ----------------------------------------------
    def load(self, params):
        self.loading = True
        try:
            self.contacts.setValue(int(params["contacts"]))
            self.contact_length.setValue(float(params["contact_length"]))
            self.gap.setValue(float(params["gap"]))
            self.diameter.setValue(float(params["diameter"]))
            self.tail.setValue(float(params["tail"]))
            if self.kind == "drg":
                self.target.setCurrentText(str(params["target"]))
                self.lateral_offset.setValue(float(params.get("lateral_offset", 0.0)))
                self.ganglion_clearance.setValue(
                    float(params.get("ganglion_clearance", 0.0)))
                self.y_offset.setValue(float(params.get("y_offset", 0.0)))
                self.z_offset.setValue(float(params.get("z_offset", 0.0)))
            else:
                self.z_center.setValue(float(params["z_center"]))
                self.x_offset.setValue(float(params["x_offset"]))
                self.level.setCurrentText(params.get("level") or CUSTOM)
        finally:
            self.loading = False
        if self.kind == "drg":
            self.describe_target()
        else:
            self.describe_offset()

    def overrides(self):
        """This page as the override dict resolve_lead() understands."""
        out = {"type": self.kind,
               "contacts": self.contacts.value(),
               "contact_length": self.contact_length.value(),
               "gap": self.gap.value(),
               "diameter": self.diameter.value(),
               "tail": self.tail.value()}
        if self.kind == "drg":
            out.update(target=self.target.currentText(),
                       lateral_offset=self.lateral_offset.value(),
                       ganglion_clearance=self.ganglion_clearance.value(),
                       y_offset=self.y_offset.value(),
                       z_offset=self.z_offset.value())
        else:
            out.update(z_center=self.z_center.value(),
                       x_offset=self.x_offset.value())
            if self.level.currentText() != CUSTOM:
                out["level"] = self.level.currentText()
        return out


class LeadDesigner(QtWidgets.QWidget):
    """The dock's contents: a set of leads, a verdict for each and for the set."""

    def __init__(self, blc):
        super(LeadDesigner, self).__init__()
        self.blc = blc
        self.cfg = blc.parse_config_file(blc.DEFAULT_CONFIGS)
        self.max_per_type = int(self.cfg.get("max_leads_per_type",
                                             blc.DEFAULT_MAX_LEADS_PER_TYPE))
        try:
            self.foramen = blc.load_foramen_corridors()["ganglia"]
        except Exception:
            self.foramen = {}
        self.ganglia = sorted(self.foramen) or ["L3"]

        self.meshes = None                  # loaded lazily; several MB of STL
        self.outcome = None                 # last validation, for Preview/Export
        self.leads = None                   # the resolved parameter sets
        self.loading = False

        outer = QtWidgets.QVBoxLayout(self)
        outer.setContentsMargins(6, 6, 6, 6)
        outer.setSpacing(6)

        # -- named configurations ----------------------------------------
        pick = QtWidgets.QHBoxLayout()
        pick.addWidget(QtWidgets.QLabel("Configuration"))
        self.pick = QtWidgets.QComboBox()
        self.pick.addItems(list(self.cfg["configs"]) + [CUSTOM])
        self.pick.setToolTip("Ready-made lead sets from lead_configs.yaml. "
                             "Changing anything below switches to custom.")
        self.pick.currentIndexChanged.connect(self.load_config)
        pick.addWidget(self.pick, 1)
        outer.addLayout(pick)

        self.note = QtWidgets.QLabel("")
        self.note.setWordWrap(True)
        self.note.setStyleSheet("color: gray;")
        outer.addWidget(self.note)

        # -- the leads ----------------------------------------------------
        add = QtWidgets.QHBoxLayout()
        add.addWidget(QtWidgets.QLabel("Add lead:"))
        self.add_buttons = {}
        for kind in ("dorsal", "ventral", "drg"):
            btn = QtWidgets.QPushButton(TYPE_WORDS[kind].split(" ")[0])
            btn.setToolTip("Add a %s lead to this configuration. At most %d of "
                           "each type." % (TYPE_WORDS[kind].lower(), self.max_per_type))
            btn.clicked.connect(lambda _c=False, k=kind: self.add_lead(k))
            add.addWidget(btn)
            self.add_buttons[kind] = btn
        self.btn_remove = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Remove this lead")
        self.btn_remove.setToolTip("Remove the lead whose tab is showing.")
        self.btn_remove.clicked.connect(self.remove_lead)
        add.addWidget(self.btn_remove)
        outer.addLayout(add)

        self.tabs = QtWidgets.QTabWidget()
        self.tabs.setDocumentMode(True)
        outer.addWidget(self.tabs)

        # -- verdict -------------------------------------------------------
        self.banner = QtWidgets.QLabel("Not checked yet")
        self.banner.setAlignment(QtCore.Qt.AlignCenter)
        self.banner.setMinimumHeight(28)
        self.set_banner(None, "Not checked yet")
        outer.addWidget(self.banner)

        self.detail = QtWidgets.QTextEdit()
        self.detail.setReadOnly(True)
        self.detail.setLineWrapMode(QtWidgets.QTextEdit.WidgetWidth)
        self.detail.setMinimumHeight(180)
        mono = QtGui.QFont("monospace")
        mono.setStyleHint(QtGui.QFont.TypeWriter)
        self.detail.setFont(mono)
        outer.addWidget(self.detail, 1)

        # -- actions -------------------------------------------------------
        row1 = QtWidgets.QHBoxLayout()
        self.btn_check = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Check fit")
        self.btn_check.setToolTip("Measure the space every lead would sit in, test "
                                  "every point on each lead's surface for being "
                                  "inside it, and measure the leads against each "
                                  "other. Takes a few seconds.")
        self.btn_check.clicked.connect(self.check)
        row1.addWidget(self.btn_check, 2)

        self.btn_preview = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Preview")
        self.btn_preview.setToolTip("Put every lead into the active document, "
                                    "replacing the last preview. Disposable -- "
                                    "do not save the document for it.")
        self.btn_preview.clicked.connect(self.do_preview)
        row1.addWidget(self.btn_preview, 1)
        outer.addLayout(row1)

        row2 = QtWidgets.QHBoxLayout()
        self.btn_clear = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Remove preview")
        self.btn_clear.setToolTip("Delete the previewed leads and put the tree "
                                  "back as it was.")
        self.btn_clear.clicked.connect(self.do_clear)
        row2.addWidget(self.btn_clear, 1)

        self.btn_export = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Export STLs")
        self.btn_export.setToolTip("Write one STL per contact plus the insulator, "
                                   "for every lead, to generated_leads/. Only "
                                   "offered for a set that fits.")
        self.btn_export.clicked.connect(self.do_export)
        row2.addWidget(self.btn_export, 1)
        outer.addLayout(row2)

        row3 = QtWidgets.QHBoxLayout()
        self.btn_rado = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Show RADO's lead")
        self.btn_rado.setToolTip(
            "Import RADO's own hand-placed 4-contact DRG lead from the five STLs "
            "it ships, as a separate disposable overlay. It is the only "
            "independently placed lead in the model, and it is what the foraminal "
            "trajectory is validated against — worth looking at beside a "
            "generated DRG lead. Not part of the anatomy; do not save it in.")
        self.btn_rado.clicked.connect(self.do_rado)
        row3.addWidget(self.btn_rado, 1)

        self.btn_rado_clear = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Hide RADO's lead")
        self.btn_rado_clear.clicked.connect(self.do_rado_clear)
        row3.addWidget(self.btn_rado_clear, 1)
        outer.addLayout(row3)

        self.status = QtWidgets.QLabel("")
        self.status.setWordWrap(True)
        self.status.setStyleSheet("color: gray;")
        outer.addWidget(self.status)

        self.load_config()

    # -- the set of pages --------------------------------------------------
    def pages(self):
        return [self.tabs.widget(i) for i in range(self.tabs.count())]

    def count_of(self, kind):
        return sum(1 for p in self.pages() if p.kind == kind)

    def retitle(self):
        """Tab labels carry the lead number, which is what the tree and the
        exported directories are named for, so they must agree."""
        for i, page in enumerate(self.pages(), start=1):
            self.tabs.setTabText(i - 1, "%d  %s" % (i, TYPE_WORDS[page.kind]))
        for kind, btn in self.add_buttons.items():
            btn.setEnabled(self.count_of(kind) < self.max_per_type)
        self.btn_remove.setEnabled(self.tabs.count() > 1)

    def add_lead(self, kind, params=None):
        if self.count_of(kind) >= self.max_per_type:
            self.status.setText(
                "This catalogue allows at most %d %s leads per configuration "
                "(max_leads_per_type in lead_configs.yaml)."
                % (self.max_per_type, kind))
            return None
        page = LeadPage(self, kind)
        if params is None:
            params = self.blc.resolve_lead(self.cfg, None, {}, {"type": kind},
                                           None, self.tabs.count() + 1, 1)
        page.load(params)
        page.changed.connect(self.went_custom)
        self.tabs.addTab(page, "")
        self.tabs.setCurrentWidget(page)
        self.retitle()
        if not self.loading:
            self.went_custom()
        return page

    def remove_lead(self):
        if self.tabs.count() <= 1:
            return
        self.tabs.removeTab(self.tabs.currentIndex())
        self.retitle()
        self.went_custom()

    # -- reading and writing the form -------------------------------------
    def load_config(self, _index=None):
        """Fill the tabs from the selected named configuration."""
        name = self.pick.currentText()
        if name == CUSTOM:
            if self.tabs.count() == 0:
                self.loading = True
                try:
                    self.add_lead("dorsal")
                finally:
                    self.loading = False
            self.note.setText("")
            return
        try:
            leads = self.blc.resolve_set(name, self.cfg)
        except Exception as exc:
            self.note.setText("cannot use this configuration: %s" % exc)
            return
        self.loading = True
        try:
            while self.tabs.count():
                self.tabs.removeTab(0)
            for params in leads:
                self.add_lead(params["type"], params)
        finally:
            self.loading = False
        self.retitle()
        self.note.setText(leads[0].get("note", ""))
        self.set_banner(None, "Not checked yet")
        self.detail.setPlainText(
            self.blc.describe_set(leads) + "\n\n"
            + "\n".join("  %s" % self.blc.describe(l) for l in leads))
        self.outcome = None

    def went_custom(self, *_a):
        """Any hand edit means this is no longer the named configuration."""
        if self.loading:
            return
        if self.pick.currentText() != CUSTOM:
            self.loading = True
            try:
                self.pick.setCurrentText(CUSTOM)
            finally:
                self.loading = False
            self.note.setText("")
        self.outcome = None
        self.set_banner(None, "Not checked yet")

    def resolve(self):
        """The tabs as a list of resolved leads.

        Each page is resolved through build_lead_config.resolve_lead() rather
        than assembled here, so the panel cannot drift from what the command
        line does and any parameter the catalogue grows is validated in exactly
        one place.
        """
        pages = self.pages()
        leads = []
        for i, page in enumerate(pages, start=1):
            leads.append(self.blc.resolve_lead(self.cfg, None, {}, {},
                                               page.overrides(), i, len(pages)))
        counts = {}
        for lead in leads:
            counts[lead["type"]] = counts.get(lead["type"], 0) + 1
        for kind, n in counts.items():
            if n > self.max_per_type:
                raise ValueError("%d %s leads, but at most %d are allowed"
                                 % (n, kind, self.max_per_type))
        return leads

    # -- actions -----------------------------------------------------------
    def set_banner(self, level, text):
        fg, bg = BANNER.get(level, ("#333333", "#e0e0e0"))
        self.banner.setText(text)
        self.banner.setStyleSheet(
            "background: %s; color: %s; border-radius: 3px; font-weight: bold;"
            % (bg, fg))

    def check(self):
        """Run the validation and show it. See the docstring on why this blocks."""
        try:
            leads = self.resolve()
        except Exception as exc:
            self.set_banner("FAIL", "Cannot build that set")
            self.detail.setPlainText(str(exc))
            return

        QtWidgets.QApplication.setOverrideCursor(QtCore.Qt.WaitCursor)
        self.status.setText("Measuring…")
        QtWidgets.QApplication.processEvents()
        try:
            if self.meshes is None:
                self.meshes = self.blc.load_meshes()
            corridor = json.load(open(self.blc.DEFAULT_CORRIDOR))
            foramen = (self.blc.load_foramen_corridors()
                       if any(l["type"] == "drg" for l in leads) else None)
            self.leads = leads
            self.outcome = self.blc.validate_set(leads, meshes=self.meshes,
                                                 corridor=corridor, foramen=foramen)
            name = self.pick.currentText()
            lines = self.blc.report_set_lines(
                "custom" if name == CUSTOM else name, leads, self.outcome)
            self.detail.setPlainText("\n".join(lines[1:]))

            levels = [lvl for r in self.outcome["leads"]
                      for lvl, _t, _m in r["checks"]]
            levels += [lvl for lvl, _t, _m in self.outcome["checks"]]
            worst = worst_of(levels)
            headline = {"PASS": "FITS", "WARN": "FITS, with a caveat",
                        "FAIL": "DOES NOT FIT"}[worst]
            if len(leads) > 1 and self.outcome["pairs"]:
                closest = min(p["gap_mm"] for p in self.outcome["pairs"])
                headline += "   —   %d leads, closest approach %.2f mm" \
                    % (len(leads), closest)
            elif self.outcome["leads"] and "clearance_mm" in self.outcome["leads"][0]["numbers"]:
                n = self.outcome["leads"][0]["numbers"]
                headline += "   —   %.2f mm lead, %+.2f mm clearance" \
                    % (leads[0]["diameter"], n["clearance_mm"])
            self.set_banner(worst, headline)
            self.status.setText("")
        except Exception:
            self.outcome = None
            self.set_banner("FAIL", "The check itself failed")
            self.detail.setPlainText(traceback.format_exc())
            self.status.setText("")
        finally:
            QtWidgets.QApplication.restoreOverrideCursor()

    def need_outcome(self):
        """Both Preview and Export work off a checked set; check if needed."""
        if self.outcome is None:
            self.check()
        return self.outcome

    def do_preview(self):
        doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
        if doc is None:
            self.status.setText("No active document to preview into.")
            return
        outcome = self.need_outcome()
        if outcome is None or not any(r.get("shapes") for r in outcome["leads"]):
            self.status.setText("Nothing to preview: no lead could be built.")
            return
        # A failing set is still previewed, on purpose -- SEEING the lead push
        # through the dura, or the two leads sitting inside each other, is the
        # clearest possible explanation of the failure.
        name = self.pick.currentText()
        try:
            _group, made = self.blc.preview_set(
                doc, "custom" if name == CUSTOM else name,
                self.leads, outcome["leads"], self.blc.lead_colours())
        except Exception as exc:
            self.status.setText("Preview failed: %s" % exc)
            return
        FreeCADGui.updateGui()
        self.status.setText("Previewed %d bodies from %d lead(s) in %s. "
                            "Disposable — do not save the document for it."
                            % (len(made), len(self.leads), doc.Label))

    def do_clear(self):
        doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
        if doc is None:
            self.status.setText("No active document.")
            return
        n = self.blc.clear_preview(doc)
        FreeCADGui.updateGui()
        self.status.setText("Removed %d preview object(s)." % n if n
                            else "There was no preview to remove.")

    def do_rado(self):
        doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
        if doc is None:
            self.status.setText("No active document.")
            return
        try:
            _g, made = self.blc.preview_rado_lead(doc, colours=self.blc.lead_colours())
        except Exception as exc:
            self.status.setText("Could not import RADO's lead: %s" % exc)
            return
        FreeCADGui.updateGui()
        self.status.setText(
            "Imported RADO's own %d-body DRG lead from STL_files/, as a "
            "reference overlay. It is not part of the anatomy — do not save the "
            "document with it in." % len(made))

    def do_rado_clear(self):
        doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
        if doc is None:
            self.status.setText("No active document.")
            return
        n = self.blc.clear_rado_lead(doc)
        FreeCADGui.updateGui()
        self.status.setText("Removed %d object(s)." % n if n
                            else "RADO's reference lead was not shown.")

    def do_export(self):
        outcome = self.need_outcome()
        if outcome is None or not all(r.get("shapes") for r in outcome["leads"]):
            self.status.setText("Nothing to export: a lead could not be built.")
            return
        if not outcome["ok"]:
            QtWidgets.QMessageBox.warning(
                self, "Lead designer",
                "This configuration does not fit, so it has not been exported."
                "\n\nThe fix is a different lead, a different position, or more "
                "space between two leads — the anatomy is not carved away to "
                "make room. See the reasons in the panel.")
            return
        name = self.pick.currentText()
        if name == CUSTOM:
            name, ok = QtWidgets.QInputDialog.getText(
                self, "Export STLs",
                "Name for this configuration (becomes the directory under "
                "generated_leads/):", text="custom_leads")
            if not ok or not name.strip():
                return
            name = name.strip()
        try:
            outdir, files = self.blc.export_set(name, self.leads, outcome["leads"],
                                                tag=name)
        except Exception as exc:
            self.status.setText("Export failed: %s" % exc)
            return
        self.status.setText("Wrote %d files to %s" % (len(files), outdir))
        QtWidgets.QMessageBox.information(
            self, "Lead designer",
            "Wrote %d STLs from %d lead(s) to\n\n%s\n\nTo keep this "
            "configuration, add an entry for it to lead_configs.yaml — the "
            "configuration plus these STLs are the durable artefact, not a saved "
            "document." % (len(files), len(self.leads), outdir))


def show_panel():
    mw = FreeCADGui.getMainWindow()
    try:
        blc = load_builder()
    except Exception as exc:
        QtWidgets.QMessageBox.critical(
            mw, "Lead designer",
            "Could not import build_lead_config.\n\n%s: %s\n\nLooked for the repo "
            "at:\n%s\n\nSet SCS_MODELING_REPO if the checkout lives somewhere else."
            % (type(exc).__name__, exc, REPO))
        return None
    try:
        panel = LeadDesigner(blc)
    except Exception:
        QtWidgets.QMessageBox.critical(mw, "Lead designer",
                                       "Could not build the panel.\n\n%s"
                                       % traceback.format_exc())
        return None

    dock = mw.findChild(QtWidgets.QDockWidget, OBJECT_NAME)
    if dock is None:
        dock = QtWidgets.QDockWidget("Lead designer", mw)
        dock.setObjectName(OBJECT_NAME)
        mw.addDockWidget(QtCore.Qt.RightDockWidgetArea, dock)
    dock.setWidget(panel)
    dock.show()
    dock.raise_()
    return dock


show_panel()
